version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-16"
abstract: >-
  FiVoHydro.jl (FiVo) solves boost-invariant relativistic viscous hydrodynamics in
  Milne coordinates together with a diffusing heavy-quark (charm) charge, in radial
  1+1D and transverse 2+1D. The bulk solvers are conservative finite volume: HLLE with
  MUSCL reconstruction in primitive variables, SSPRK2/3 time stepping, operator-split
  relaxation of the dissipative fields, and a MOOD fallback. The charm second-moment
  solver, whose equations have no conservative form, is integrated in quasi-linear
  form with RK4. It ships a validation
  ladder in which every gate is judged by a referee that is not the code under test —
  a closed form, a semi-analytic ODE, or a second, independently written solver.
keywords:
  - relativistic hydrodynamics
  - heavy-ion collisions
  - heavy-quark diffusion
  - Israel-Stewart
  - finite volume
  - Julia
